{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I missed my morning insulin two days ago. Then I had a big glass of sweet tea on the way to my doctor’s appointment, and my blood sugar was over 500 when I got there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And your doctor called you later with even higher results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they said my blood sugar was 800. They told me to come here right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s very high. You’ve been feeling tired, thirsty, and urinating a lot, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all of that. But no nausea, pain, or fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good, no signs of infection or DKA this time. Your labs show a blood sugar of 754, but no ketones. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m not in DKA again? I was so scared after last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, you’re not in DKA now. But your diabetes is still not well controlled. Your last A1c was 12%, which is quite high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I’ve been struggling with remembering my insulin, especially since I’ve been feeling down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2157-08-25 01:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aware of that. Your depression is important to manage too. For now, we’re going to adjust your insulin to help prevent this from happening again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2157-08-25 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve consulted the diabetes team. They’re changing your insulin. You’ll stop NPH and start Lantus at bedtime—32 units."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2157-08-25 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lantus? Is that different from what I was on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2157-08-25 02:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Lantus is a long-acting insulin once a day. It’s more stable than NPH. You’ll also use Humalog as a sliding scale with meals to cover highs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2157-08-25 02:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds simpler. But I’m nervous about giving myself more shots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2157-08-25 02:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll teach you how to use the insulin pens. They’re easy—just dial and inject. A nurse will show you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still tired, but my mouth isn’t as dry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar this morning was 240—much better than 754. The new insulin is starting to work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my kidney numbers? Last time they were worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine was 1.5 on admission, which is high for you—your baseline is 0.6. But it’s already down to 1.1 today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So is it getting better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. It was likely due to dehydration from high sugars. You’re urinating a lot, which supports that. But it may have caused some kidney injury, so you’ll follow up with nephrology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2157-08-25 08:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I have an appointment next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2157-08-25 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nutritionist stopped by. Did she talk to you about your diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2157-08-25 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she did. I didn’t realize sweet tea could spike my sugar so much. I’ll switch to water or unsweetened tea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2157-08-25 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. Small changes like that, plus the new insulin, should help a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2157-08-25 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, can you check my wounds? They feel a little sore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2157-08-25 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let me take a look. The ulcer on your abdomen has a little drainage, but it’s healing. The one in your left gluteal fold is clean, no redness or pus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2157-08-25 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not infected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2157-08-25 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, no signs of infection. We’ll keep doing daily dressing changes, just like at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. Your blood sugar is now 140, and your creatinine is stable at 1.1. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take Lantus 32 units at bedtime. Use Humalog before meals based on your blood sugar—here’s the sliding scale."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And stop the NPH completely?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, stop NPH. We’re also giving you a new insulin pen, a glucometer, and test strips. Check your sugar three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my wounds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Home health will continue dressing changes. You have surgery follow-up for those. And keep taking your Paxil for depression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the kidney doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2157-08-26 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, keep that appointment. They’ll check a microalbumin to see how your kidneys are doing long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2157-08-26 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Everything looks good. You’re cleared to go home. A walker will help you stay steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2157-08-26 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll try not to miss my insulin again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2157-08-26 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Call your PCP if your sugars go above 300 or if you feel unwell. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2157-08-26 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2157-08-25 01:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2157-08-26 17:44:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with type II diabetes, hypertension, and depression, was admitted for severe hyperglycemia with a blood glucose of 754 mg/dL after missing her morning NPH insulin and consuming sweetened tea. She did not have diabetic ketoacidosis. Her insulin regimen was changed from NPH to glargine 32 units at bedtime with a humalog sliding scale due to poor glycemic control and prior hypoglycemia. She received nutrition counseling and education on insulin pen use. Her creatinine improved from 1.5 to 1.1 mg/dL, likely due to resolution of prerenal acute kidney injury, and she has follow-up scheduled with nephrology. Skin abscesses from a prior admission were monitored, remained clean without infection, and continued on outpatient wound care. She was discharged home with home health services, new insulin therapy, and follow-up arranged for diabetes, surgery, and kidney function.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Severe nonproliferative diabetic retinopathy",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Nonspecific abnormal results of function study of kidney",
      "Cellulitis and abscess of trunk",
      "Hypopotassemia"
    ]
  }
}
